{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>When they have a matter.</b> That is, when a dispute arises among those leading men who handle public affairs." "<b>They come to me, and I judge between a man and his fellow.</b> Between those great men of the generation who handle public affairs." "<b>And I make known the statutes of Elohim and His teachings.</b> To those great men, so that they may know them — as it says: וַיָּשֻׁבוּ אֵלָיו אַהֲרֹן וְכָל הַנְּשִׂיאִים בָּעֵדָה, וְאַחַר כֵן נִגְּשׁוּ כָּל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Exodus 34:31–32). And as they said, of blessed memory (Eruvin 54b): 'What is the order of Mishnah?' For these three reasons the people had to wait from morning until evening, until the great men departed and I could turn to judge the common folk."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:09.540301583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}